• It always works with the OVER() clause.
• It assigns a rank to each row based on the ORDER BY clause.
• It assigns a rank to each row in consecutive order.
• It always assigns a rank to rows, starting with one for each new partition.
• SQL Server provides the following rank functions:
• RANK()
• ROW_NUMBER()
• DENSE_RANK()
• NTILE()
 
• RANK():
• This function is used to determine the rank for each row in the result set. 
• It allows duplicate ranks
• It gives similar rank if they have same value.
•  
•  
• ROW_NUMBER()
•  It will gives the different ranks for the row having similar values
• It doesn't allows duplicate ranks.
•  
 
DENSE_RANK() Function
It always specifies ranking in consecutive order. If we get a duplicate value, this function will assign it with the same rank, and the next rank being the next sequential number. This characteristic differs DENSE_RANK() function from the RANK() function.
 